WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aif_111'), 'The launch plan estimated hint tokens as words / 0.75, a ratio measured on English hints. Before the Vietnamese launch, a developer counted one hint in both languages with the hint model''s own token counter:

lang  words  estimated tokens (words / 0.75)  counted tokens
en    96     128                              131
vi    124    165                              338

Statement: "Applying the ratio measured on English hints to Vietnamese hints gives a token estimate close to the real count."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The ratio worked for English (128 estimated, 131 counted) but underestimated the Vietnamese hint by about half (165 estimated, 338 counted). A tokenizer splits text into pieces from a vocabulary built mostly from English text, so Vietnamese syllables with diacritics are often split into several tokens. The words-to-tokens rule of thumb is a property of English prose with one tokenizer, not of language in general. The fix is to count real samples per language with the tokenizer of the model you call, and to budget each language separately. The misconception is that a token is roughly a word in every language.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aif_111') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
