WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aif_311'), 'Evidence D - support-bot request log:
2026-10-20T21:14:07.418Z support-bot req=sb_77f3 user=u_5521 model=chat-small-2025-01 knowledge_cutoff=2025-01 temperature=0.2 input_tokens=41 output_tokens=58 docs_attached=0 finish_reason=stop latency_ms=1840

Statement: "The temperature is the cause: with temperature 0 the model would have given the correct 2.x call instead of inventing an option."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Temperature controls how often the model picks a less likely token; 0.2 is already low. At temperature 0 it always picks the most likely token, but without the docs in the prompt the most likely answer is still a guess, so you would get the same wrong answer every time. Lowering the temperature makes an answer repeatable, not true. The misconception is that hallucinations are random noise that sampling settings can turn off; here the missing facts are the cause.', 4, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aif_311') AND order_index = 4)
    RETURNING id
)
INSERT INTO challenge.question_options (question_id, option_text, is_correct)
SELECT q.id, o.option_text, o.is_correct
FROM q, (VALUES
        ('True', false),
        ('False', true)
    ) AS o(option_text, is_correct);
WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aif_311'), 'Evidence B - prompt log, request sb_77f3 (the full prompt):
You are the CodeDev support assistant. Be friendly and answer the learner''s question.

Question: How do I submit my lesson when one hidden test still fails?

Evidence C - https://app.codedev.test/docs/lab/submit:
submitLesson({ lessonId, attemptId })                      @codedev/lab 2.x
  lessonId   string   the lesson to submit
  attemptId  string   the attempt created by `codedev test`
An attempt with a failing test is rejected (status "rejected", failedTests listed).
Tests cannot be skipped: fix the test, run `codedev test` again and submit the new attemptId.
CHANGELOG
2.0.0  2025-09-15  submitLesson(lessonId) is replaced by submitLesson({ lessonId, attemptId })
1.4.0  2024-11-02  codedev test prints the attempt id
1.0.0  2024-03-11  first release: submitLesson(lessonId)

Statement: "A prompt that contains the docs page from C with an id such as [lab-submit-v2], tells the model to answer only from that documentation and cite the id, and allows "I''m not sure" when the docs do not answer, closes the gaps that produced force: true."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Each part closes one gap. The docs page brings the current signature into the context window, so the knowledge cutoff no longer matters for this question. "Answer only from the documentation and cite the id" makes the answer checkable: the widget can link the citation and a test can verify it. The allowed "I''m not sure" gives the model a correct reply when retrieval finds nothing, instead of pressure to invent one. The common shortcut - adding "do not hallucinate" without the docs - adds no facts at all.', 5, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aif_311') AND order_index = 5)
    RETURNING id
)
