WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aif_311'), 'Evidence A - support widget, conversation sb_77f3:
21:14:02  learner u_5521  How do I submit my lesson when one hidden test still fails?
21:14:07  support bot     You can force the submission. Call submitLesson({ lessonId, force: true }) from your lab script: the force flag skips the hidden tests and marks the lesson as submitted. It has been supported since @codedev/lab 1.4.
21:31:40  learner u_5521  I tried it: CodeDevLabError: submitLesson: unknown option "force" (expected { lessonId, attemptId }). What now?

Verification note in the fix''s pull request:
"Tested on staging: asked ''How do I submit my lesson when one hidden test still fails?'' once, got the 2.x call with [lab-submit-v2]. Closing ticket #2291."

Statement: "This check is enough to show that the incident is fixed and will not come back."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. One question, asked once, checks one path. It does not check a question the docs do not cover (the bot must say "I''m not sure" there, not invent), it says nothing about the next run if the temperature is above 0, and it will not run again when someone changes the prompt builder. Verification is a small eval set of real questions - each with the source it must cite or the expectation "I''m not sure" - run on recorded fixtures in CI and on the live model before each release. The misconception is to treat one good answer as proof.', 6, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aif_311') AND order_index = 6)
    RETURNING id
)
